    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/AB201C499D53A5D603D5BE296513B383/jobs/404161": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Athletic Trainer - 10 Month (Anticipated Opening) (30068) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Athletic Trainer - 10 Month (Anticipated Opening) (30068) Ottawa University - Ottawa, Kansas - Ottawa, KS 66067 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Travel Percentage Yes - Driving MVR Required Category Sports Apply Description OUR UNIVERSITY Ottawa University (established in 1865), one of the oldest private liberal arts universities in the United States, is a multi-campus system serving approximately 4000 students through its campuses in Kansas (Ottawa, Kansas- Residential Campus and Overland Park, Kansas- Adult Programs); Arizona (Surprise Residential Campus and OUAZ Adult Programs); Wisconsin (Brookfield Adult Programs); and our OU ONLINE PROGRAM based out of Overland Park, Kansas. Ottawa University is a regionally accredited, church-related, private university that strives to integrate faith, learning, and life in the academic experiences of students. JOB SUMMARY Responsible for performing all facets of the sports medicine program and the operation of the athletic training room on a 10-month schedule.  Works with student-athletes in all sports toward prevention, care, and rehabilitation of all athletic related injuries. Position requires a high level of interaction with varied groups, individual judgment and discretion. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB (provide list of items which are essential to effective outcomes in this role): Regular and effective prevention and care of athletic injury and illness.  Support the implementation of the athletic training program working closely with the director, athletic administration, coaches, faculty, staff, and students associated with the athletic training program. Provide coverage at all home athletic events, practices and appropriate away events; work effectively with full-time staff and part-time work study student-trainers & scholarship student-trainers; maintain and build working relationships with appropriate doctors and medical facilities. Evaluate injuries of student-athletes; administer proper care and/or referral to medical personnel; recommend training regimens for athletes; determine an appropriate timeframe for an athlete to return to competitive practices and effectively communicate that plan with the coaches and student-athletes. Oversee the monitoring and care of the athletics training room, equipment, and inventory housed there. Maintain appropriate documentation and record keeping. Maintain the system of daily records of assessments, treatments, and rehabilitation on all athletes with guaranteed confidentiality according to FERPA, HIPPA, and others that apply. Responsible for athletic insurance related recordkeeping and communications. Coordinate NAIA Drug Education policies and procedures with staff and student-athletes Stay current with certification, and the most current athletic training practices and procedures that are pertinent to the evaluation, care and rehabilitation of injuries. Responsible for maintaining a high degree of confidentiality with student-athletes and medical matters including, but not limited to HIPAA and FERPA regulations. Other duties as assigned STANDARD UNIVERSITY EXPECTATIONS: Model and encourage collaboration among University departments assuring effective communication and operations. Understand the University's policies and, procedures, and exercise good judgment accordingly. Assure that University and student information is managed in a confidential and ethical manner in accordance with the Universitys Code of Conduct and Ethics. Provide leadership through conduct, attitude, and professionalism. Represent the University to students, external groups, faculty, and staff in a way that reflects positively on the University. Be mindful and supportive of the overall Mission of Ottawa University. Exercise Inclusivity in your daily actions accruing alignment within expectations of the University’s Mission Statement and Statement of Inclusion, Openness, and Community. NOTE This job description in no way states or implies that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee(s) incumbent in this position. Employees will be required to follow any other job-related instructions and to perform any other job-related duties requested by any person authorized to give instructions or assignments. All duties and responsibilities are essential functions and requirements and are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate individuals with disabilities. To perform this job successfully, the incumbents will possess the skills, aptitudes, and abilities to perform each duty proficiently. Some requirements may exclude individuals who pose a direct threat or significant risk to the health or safety of themselves or others. The requirements listed in this document are the minimum levels of knowledge, skills, or abilities. This document does not create an employment contract, implied or otherwise, other than an at will relationship . Ottawa University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not unlawfully discriminate in recruitment or employment on the basis of race, age, sex, color, religion, disability, national origin, sexual orientation, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by law. Qualifications REQUIRED EDUCATION: (education based on essential job duties and requirements consistent with business necessity): Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred.  Current athletic trainer certification is required.Must also be in good standing with the National Athletic Trainers Association and have Kansas Licensure or eligibility to apply and receive it. REQUIRED EXPERIENCE: ( experience based on requirements in role and are consistent with business necessity) Prior experience, prefer collegiate level experience. ADDITIONAL ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS: List required and/or preferred certification, industry specific requirements, required or preferred use of equipment, and all necessary job skills, abilities, and knowledge competencies) Provide a list of items below: Current/valid Driver’s License Effective interpersonal, communication and motivation skills Ability to think critically and provide options for sound solutions Ability to manage individuals and complex tasks Positive role model for student-athletes, university personnel, alumni, and members of the off- campus community. WORKING CONDITIONS (Physical attributes required to perform job duties with or without reasonable accommodation - examples: sitting, lifting #, bending, driving, environmental factors or elements, noise level, stairs in a building, or other factors that will affect working conditions). Provide a list of items below: Maintain emotional control under stress. Frequent standing, stooping, bending, pulling, pushing, and lifting; frequent prolonged and irregular hours, and exposure to varying temperatures. TRAVEL REQUIREMENTS: Yes - Travel Required If YES, list type and approximate percentage: Regular requirement for this position Responsible for driving students and University vehicles as part of job duties (YES/NO): Yes Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/AB201C499D53A5D603D5BE296513B383/jobs/413260": {
      "title": "Campus Pastor (PT)",
      "description": "Campus Pastor (PT) (29995) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Campus Pastor (PT) (29995) Ottawa University - Surprise, Arizona - Surprise, AZ 85374 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Over 20 Hours Travel Percentage No - Driving MVR Category Social Service Apply Description Responsible for establishing a dynamic Christian campus faith development program applicable to all students and employees. This position plays an integral role in leading the spiritual development of a religiously diverse campus, as well as fostering personal faith. Essential Functions: Responsible for all components of Spirit Life, including scheduling speakers, providing leadership to the praise band, monitoring attendance, and collaborating with OUAZ TV. Serves as the spiritual leader of the campus and establishes programming for Sprit Life. Creates a dynamic campus Christian faith development program which provides opportunities for personal growth and exploration for traditional-age students with varying interests in personal faith. Works to educate the larger student body to understand what it means to have an enlightened faith, and then understand how this faith can impact and inform life. Develops programs (exploration, relationship building, and creative) that provide opportunities for interested students to explore personal Christian faith through co-curricular and spiritual activities, following a dynamic and engaging format, including, but not limited to discipleship, faith journeys, scripture study, worship services, and programs around faith development. Provides opportunities for students interested in ministry and leadership to serve and support others through a dynamic campus leadership program, including ministry-related career planning and internship opportunities. Models the Christian faith through conduct, attitude, and professionalism.  Setting a standard and tone which creates excitement in everyday student life and reflects positively on the Christian faith, the University, and this program. Provides ministerial counseling and advising to students as needed.  Coordinates Christian counseling-related activities, in cooperation with the Campus Counselor, as deemed appropriate.  Assures policy and parameters are in place, through collaborative work with the Counselor, to assure students with needs are served. Recommends policy changes and develops procedures to improve the unit’s operations. Other duties as assigned Qualifications Required Education: Bachelor's Degree, Master's Preferred. Required Experience: Five years of applicable leadership/campus ministry experience required. Additional Eligibility Requirements: A caring and compassionate person, who maintains a positive and engaging personality, and relates to and thrives on the development of college students seeking growth and support. Demonstrates a strength in mentoring and leading others toward personal and spiritual development. Excellent communication skills and sincere willingness to be actively involved in the lives of students. Experience fostering initiative, as well as leading individuals and groups. Maintains interest and enthusiasm by getting involved and effectively leading faith programming (collaboratively) across the community:  residence halls, athletic teams, intramurals, non-traditional students, etc. Working Conditions: (Physical attributes required to perform job duties with or without reasonable accommodation - examples: sitting, lifting, bending, driving, environmental factors or elements, noise level, stairs in a building, or other factors that will affect working conditions) May require evening and weekend activities for events and meetings. Prolonged periods of sitting must be able to lift 5-15 pounds at times. Travel Requirements: If travel is required, list type and approximate percentage: None Responsible for driving students and University vehicles as part of job duties: No Standard University Expectations: Be mindful and supportive of the Mission of Ottawa University. Understand and follow the University’s policies and procedures and exercise good judgment accordingly. Assure that University and student information is managed in a confidential and ethical manner in accordance with the University’s Code of Conduct and Ethics. Manage your staff in accordance with University personnel policies. Encourage collaboration among the staff, provide regular evaluation and feedback, and facilitate developmental opportunities. Model and encourage collaboration among University offices and campuses assuring effective communication and operations. Provide leadership through conduct, attitude, and professionalism. Represent the University to students, external groups, faculty, and staff in a way that reflects positively on the University. Exercise inclusivity in your daily actions in accordance with the University’s Mission Statement, Statement of Spiritual Identity, and Statement of Inclusion, Openness, and Community. Our University Ottawa University “prepares professional and liberal arts graduates for lifetimes of personal significance, vocational fulfillment, and service to God and humanity” from residential campuses in Ottawa, Kansas (established 1865) and Surprise, Arizona (established 2017) and from professional and online campuses in Kansas City, Phoenix, and Milwaukee. Ottawa University is a regionally accredited, church-related, student-centered, private comprehensive university that strives to integrate faith, learning, and life in the academic experiences of students. This job description in no way states or implies that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee(s) incumbent in this position. Employees will be required to follow any other job-related instructions and to perform any other job-related duties requested by any person authorized to give instructions or assignments. All duties and responsibilities are essential functions and requirements and are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate individuals with disabilities. To perform this job successfully, the incumbents will possess the skills, aptitudes, and abilities to perform each duty proficiently. Some requirements may exclude individuals who pose a direct threat or significant risk to the health or safety of themselves or others. The requirements listed in this document are the minimum levels of knowledge, skills, or abilities. This document does not create an employment contract, implied or otherwise, other than an “at will” relationship. Ottawa University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not unlawfully discriminate in recruitment or employment on the basis of race, age, sex, color, religion, disability, national origin, sexual orientation, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/AB201C499D53A5D603D5BE296513B383/jobs/412502": {
      "title": "Community Development Executive",
      "description": "Community Development Executive - OP (30332) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Community Development Executive - OP (30332) Ottawa University - Overland Park, Kansas - Overland Park, KS 66211 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Travel Percentage Yes - Driving MVR Required Category Sales Apply Description Responsible for administration of an effective community recruitment program and associated processes which are aligned with Ottawa University’s student centric philosophy.  Responsible for developing relationships and measurable qualified student leads through feeder schools and/or corporate/community partnerships for our online markets specifically. Also, provides support to the overall community and corporate relations strategy. Maintains relationships established as a Community Development Executive, within a specific community or vertical, and refines/develops these relationships toward building meaningful and enrollment partnerships. Local and regional travel required. Essential Functions: Provides daily support of comprehensive community relations strategy. Coordinates campus outreach strategy, working in conjunction with department/campus leaders and other Community Development Executives.  Expands on, and further develops these relationships toward meaningful enrollment partnerships. Responsible for development, implementation, tracking, and assessment of organized plans for recruiting new students and cultivating relationships with key external constituents.  Remains in communication with key external constituents to ensure the continuation or expansion of these relationships. Responsible for formalizing strategic alliances with specific academic programs/schools to create streamlined pathways from associate’s to bachelor’s to master’s degree. Responsible for identifying and coordinating opportunities for when additional Ottawa team members could support an Outreach function. Responsible for assuring the accuracy and appropriate distribution of campus marketing material. Responsible for scheduling student generating events on a weekly basis to ensure the campus/unit is on track to hit enrollment targets. Work with departmental/campus leaders to establish meaningful and measurable enrollment goals, and monitoring performance against those goals.  Responsible for generating a pre-determined number of targeted leads to meet term and annual enrollment goals. Maintains close working relations with supporting offices including financial aid, registrar’s office, business office and academic advisors to ensure a smooth and successful enrollment process for students and to provide accurate information and meet student expectations. Advises external constituents concerning University program options in relation to making the decision of which program(s) will most closely fit their background, strengths, needs, and preferences. Responsible for the accurate and timely entry of all data pertaining to outreach activities into database. Prepares reports as requested (weekly/monthly/quarterly/annually) and/or as needed. Coordinates with Registrar to develop and maintain transfer guides and articulation agreements with feeder school partners. Represents OU to the external community through engagement in community events, civic organizations, and associations with the goal of increasing brand awareness and generating referrals for new student enrollment Occasionally calls graduation or community college lead lists. Other duties as assigned Qualifications Required Education: Bachelor’s Degree required.  Master’s Degree or equivalent experience preferred. Required Experience: Minimum one year related experience in recruiting or sales. Additional Eligibility Requirements: Customer Service orientation with strong written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated experience with leveraging a CRM tool to guide and track day-to-day activities Experience in developing professional contacts, relationships, and lead generation through personal contact, as well as contact via telephone and other electronic means Ability to facilitate resolution of problems; effectively meet time sensitive deadlines Must possess the skills to self-initiate and manage a diverse set of activities/duties with accuracy, organization and attention to detail Proficiency with a PC including, Word, Excel and student database systems Ability to work independently, make sound decisions, and effectively manage time Effectively lead others toward closure/decisions Working Conditions: (Physical attributes required to perform job duties with or without reasonable accommodation - examples: sitting, lifting, bending, driving, environmental factors or elements, noise level, stairs in a building, or other factors that will affect working conditions) Tasks involve the ability to exert light physical effort in sedentary to light work. This may involve some lifting, carrying, moving, pushing and/or pulling of objects/materials of light weight (up to 50 pounds). Work occasional irregular hours, including some nights and weekends. Articulate verbal communication with students, faculty and staff expected. Travel is expected. Tasks may involve extended periods of time at a keyboard or workstation. Travel Requirements: If travel is required, list type and approximate percentage: 75-80% Local and regional travel associated with student recruitment and community partnership building Responsible for driving students and University vehicles as part of job duties: No Standard University Expectations: Be mindful and supportive of the Mission of Ottawa University Understand and follow the University’s policies and procedures and exercise good judgment accordingly. Assure that University and student information is managed in a confidential and ethical manner in accordance with the University’s Code of Conduct and Ethics. Manage your staff in accordance with University personnel policies. Encourage collaboration among the staff, provide regular evaluation and feedback, and facilitate developmental opportunities. Model and encourage collaboration among University offices and campuses assuring effective communication and operations. Provide leadership through conduct, attitude, and professionalism. Represent the University to students, external groups, faculty, and staff in a way that reflects positively on the University. Exercise inclusivity in your daily actions in accordance with the University’s Mission Statement, Statement of Spiritual Identity, and Statement of Inclusion, Openness, and Community. Our University Ottawa University “prepares professional and liberal arts graduates for lifetimes of personal significance, vocational fulfillment, and service to God and humanity” from residential campuses in Ottawa, Kansas (established 1865) and Surprise, Arizona (established 2017) and from professional and online campuses in Kansas City, Phoenix, and Milwaukee. Ottawa University is a regionally accredited, church-related, student-centered, private comprehensive university that strives to integrate faith, learning, and life in the academic experiences of students. This job description in no way states or implies that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee(s) incumbent in this position. Employees will be required to follow any other job-related instructions and to perform any other job-related duties requested by any person authorized to give instructions or assignments. All duties and responsibilities are essential functions and requirements and are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate individuals with disabilities. To perform this job successfully, the incumbents will possess the skills, aptitudes, and abilities to perform each duty proficiently. Some requirements may exclude individuals who pose a direct threat or significant risk to the health or safety of themselves or others. The requirements listed in this document are the minimum levels of knowledge, skills, or abilities. This document does not create an employment contract, implied or otherwise, other than an “at will” relationship. Ottawa University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not unlawfully discriminate in recruitment or employment on the basis of race, age, sex, color, religion, disability, national origin, sexual orientation, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
